    "title": "Where to watch LSU vs. Duke in March Madness Sweet 16: Time, TV Channel",
    "text": "Updated March 27, 2026, 9:08 a.m. ETMarch Madness is underway and college basketball's big dance continues with No. 2 seed LSU taking on No. 3 seed Duke in a Sweet 16 matchup on Friday, March 27. Here's everything you need to know to tune in for the clash between the Blue Devils and Lady Tigers.USA TODAY Sports has a team of journalists covering women's March Madness to keep you up to date with every point scored, rebound grabbed and game won in the 68-team tournament.USA TODAY Studio IX : Check out our women's sports hub for in-depth analysis, commentary and moreWatch LSU vs. Duke with Fubo free trialWhat time is Duke vs LSU Sweet 16 game?No. 2 LSU vs No. 3 Duke tips off at 10:00 PM (EST) on Friday, March 27 from Golden 1 Center (Sacramento, California).What channel is Duke vs LSU Sweet 16 game?No. 2 LSU vs No. 3 Duke is airing live on ESPN (watch free with Fubo).How to stream Duke vs LSU Sweet 16 gameNo. 2 LSU vs No. 3 Duke is available to stream on Fubo.Watch LSU vs. Duke free with FuboDuke March Madness resultsRound of 62: def No. 14 Charleston, 81-64Round of 32: def No. 6 Baylor, 69-46LSU March Madness resultsRound of 32: def No. 7 Texas Tech, 101-47Round of 62: def No. 15 Jacksonville, 116-58Women's March Madness schedule todaySee the schedule, live scores and results for all of Friday's NCAA Tournament action here.Watch the NCAA Tournament all March long with Fubo2026 Women's NCAA Tournament full scheduleMarch 18-19: First FourMarch 20-21: First RoundMarch 22-23: Second RoundMarch 27-28: Sweet 16March 29-30: Elite 8April 3: Final FourApril 5: National ChampionshipJoin the USA TODAY Survivor Pool to win cash prizesOur team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.Information in this article was imported automatically into a template written and reviewed by a USA TODAY Sports editor. You